uropathy: possible but less likely to explain pain profile", "Thoracic outlet syndrome: consider after neurological localization", "Pancoast tumor syndrome: possible given apical risk factors and weight loss but requires imaging confirmation"], "alarm_features": ["17-pound weight loss (suspicious for malignancy/metabolism)", "Chronic alcohol/smoking use (systemic risk factors)", "Hypertension (177/108 mmHg)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Brachial Plexopathy", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.4189818571018198, "danger": 0.3, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["The absence of trauma or radiation weakly supports brachial plexopathy over traumatic causes but does not rule out non-traumatic plexopathy."], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B1.1", "B1.2", "B1.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.4, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Cerebrovascular Disease", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.28789322217026236, "danger": 0.5, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Hypertension is a known cerebrovascular risk factor but provides only weak support for stroke due to the subacute presentation, which is atypical for acute cer…"], "evidence_against": ["Subacute progression weakly contradicts cerebral infarction, which usually has acute onset, but does not exclude chronic stroke variants."], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1", "B2.2", "B2.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.6, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "la